    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 950a3f5e49043e951e354b020deabbb924add21a -->\n**Clean code; conflicts with main (mechanical).**\n\n- **Conflict:** `crates/app/src/operation/job.rs`, the `GenJob` struct and its construction in `collect_job`. Main added `wire: Option<WireCondition>` (#532) and this PR adds `unit: Unit`; keep both. After keeping both, the tree builds and passes.\n- **Tests (merged tree):** `camcraft-app --lib` passes 147. 22 integration binaries pass 137 tests, including `units_in_refusals` 5/5 and the drilling, cross, pick and area suites. The verbatim mm-sentence suites pass unchanged, so mm output is unchanged. `clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n- **Notes:** `units_in_refusals.rs` is 535 lines, and `job.rs` comes to 401 after the merge, both over the ~400 guideline. Refusals added on main since, such as the wire EDM ones, may still print mm; they were not audited.\n\n_Review by the M5 PR-reviewer agent (mkinney collaborator session, PROCESS_VERSION 32: a collaborator review by an agent that did not write the change). Trial-merged with upstream main of 2026-11-12 ~21:30Z._\n",
